The ingredients are: Strong white bread flour 500 g; Caster sugar 70 g; Instant dried yeast 8 g; Fine sea salt 9 g; Whole eggs 250 g; Whole milk (32 C) 100 g; Unsalted butter, softened 225 g; Dark chocolate chips 150 g.
The method is: Whisk the flour, sugar, yeast and salt together dry, then beat in the eggs and warm milk until the dough climbs the hook and cleans the bowl. Add the softened butter in five additions, waiting for each to disappear before the next. Fold the chocolate chips through by hand at the very end, or the paddle will smash them into the crumb and grey the whole loaf. Chill overnight at 4 C. Scale into a lined tin the next morning, prove until risen by half, and bake at 180 C for 35 minutes.
The oven setting is 180 C.
Allergen warning: Contains wheat (gluten), egg, dairy and soy (from the chocolate).
